     "upgrade_note": "This device's agent speaks protocol v31; v0.0.7 speaks v26, so installing it would lower the device's protocol and lose what needs v27–v31. The hub runs an unreleased build (dev+g0a796d2.dirty), and the Executors panel's Upgrade button and auto-update install published releases only. To move the device forward, build cloop from the hub's own uncommitted source tree (on commit 0a796d2), in a full clone, as a static binary (`CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -ldflags \"-X github.com/blechschmidt/cloop/pkg/version.Commit=$(git rev-parse HEAD) -X github.com/blechschmidt/cloop/pkg/version.Sequence=$(git rev-list --count --first-parent HEAD)\" -o cloop .`), copy it to the device and run `sudo ./cloop executor agent install --upgrade --insecure-skip-verify` there (a binary built by hand carries no signed provenance); a plain --upgrade keeps the device's packet-filter grant as it is.",
     "rollback_note": "This device's agent runs dev+g0a796d2.dirty, a build that carries no place on main, so its installer has nothing to order an upgrade by: rollback protection does not cover it, and a forced upgrade could still move it to any older release. Its agent cannot carry out an upgrade the hub asks for, so upgrade it once on the device, as root: `cloop upgrade` fetches the latest release (v0.0.7 or later) and verifies its signature, then `cloop executor agent install --upgrade --remote-upgrade` restarts the agent on it and installs the helper the Upgrade button needs. From then on its installer refuses any build earlier than the one it runs.",
